CM A plane-wave EX standing BEFORE the driven voltage source, with NTHETA/NPHI
CM that collide with a real (tag, segment) on the wire.
CM
CM A plane wave has no feedpoint: its tag/segment fields carry NTHETA and NPHI.
CM Frontends that took "the first EX card" therefore reported segment 3 — a grid
CM dimension — as the antenna feedpoint, where the CLI reported segment 26.
CM
CM Fixture for the FND-031 feedpoint seam. The feedpoint is tag 1 segment 26.
CM
CM This deck is REFUSED since FND-050, and pins the refusal's text rather than a
CM solved value. It carries two drive kinds at once, which fnec will not solve --
CM and neither does NEC-2: nec2c answers it 79.348 + j46.223, bit-identical to
CM the same deck with the plane wave deleted, so the reference discards rather
CM than superposes. Before the refusal the three frontends gave three different
CM answers for it, none flagged.
CM
CM Assert that the refusal names tag 1 segment 26 -- the driven source, not the
CM plane wave's NTHETA/NPHI. That is the same FND-031 fact this fixture always
CM pinned; only the place it is read from has moved.
CE
GW 1 51 0 0 -5.282 0 0 5.282 0.001
GE 0
EX 1 1 3 0 0.0 0.0
EX 0 1 26 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 1 0 0 14.2 0
EN
